</h1><gml:sk n="0.75" unit="line" break="yes"/>Normal filled text that goes on for a while so that it wraps at least
once in the justified paragraph mode of the formatter.
<gml:in left="4" unit="ch" break="yes"/>Indented by four characters, still in the same paragraph? No: .in breaks.
<gml:in left="4ch+1i" unit="mixed" delta="+1i" break="yes"/>A mixed indent of four characters plus one inch.
<gml:in left="0" unit="ch" break="yes"/><gml:ir right="10" unit="mh" break="yes"/>Right margin pulled in by ten ems so that this text wraps earlier than the
others do on the page.
<gml:ir right="0" unit="ch" break="yes"/><gml:sp n="2" unit="line" break="yes"/>After two blank lines.
<gml:sk n="1" unit="line" break="yes"/><gml:sk n="2" unit="line" break="yes"/>After skips of one and two lines: only the larger counts.
<gml:lines word="ce" n="2" break="yes">These two lines
are centered.</gml:lines>
<gml:lines word="ri" n="on" break="yes">Flush right one
flush right two
</gml:lines><gml:fo fill="no" align="left" overdraw="extend" break="yes"/>No fill: this line
and this line
  are kept as lines.
<gml:fo fill="yes" align="justify" overdraw="extend" break="yes"/><gml:fo fill="yes" align="center" overdraw="extend" break="yes"/>Centered fill mode text.
<gml:fo fill="yes" align="justify" overdraw="extend" break="yes"/><gml:lines word="us" n="2" break="no">Underscored words here
and here</gml:lines>
<gml:lines word="up" n="1" break="no">Upper case line with café</gml:lines>
Back to normal.
<gml:in left="5" unit="ch" after="1" after-unit="line" break="yes"/>First line at the old margin, then the following lines are indented by
five characters until the margin changes again, which is right now.
<gml:in left="0" unit="ch" break="yes"/><gml:il shift="3" unit="mh" break="yes"/>An indented first line in a paragraph that is long enough to wrap onto a
second line so the effect can be seen.
<gml:of offset="4" unit="ch" break="yes"/>Offset: the first line is at the margin and every following line is
indented by four characters, for this paragraph and the next.
<gml:br break="yes"/>Next paragraph still offset by the .of control word, all of its lines.
<gml:in left="0" unit="ch" offset="0" break="yes"/><gml:bf font="hi2" break="no"/>Bold from a font change,
<gml:bf font="hi1" break="no"/>italic inside it<gml:pf font="hi2" break="no"/>,
<gml:pf initial="yes" break="no"/>and back to the initial font.
<gml:df name="big" spec="type(bold italic)" break="no"/><gml:bf font="big" break="no"/>Defined bold italic font.
<gml:pf initial="yes" break="no"/><gml:tp action="set" stops="10mh 20mh 30mh" break="yes"/><gml:fo fill="no" align="left" overdraw="extend" break="yes"/>Name	Value	Note
